<&_ if (fragment.testingSection) { -&>
#### Playwright E2E tests

UI end-to-end tests are also powered by [Playwright][]. They're located in [<%= playwrightDir %>](<%= playwrightDir %>).

Install the browsers once:

```
npx playwright install --with-deps <%- playwrightBrowsers.join(' ') %>
```

Then start Spring Boot in one terminal (`<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run app:start`) and run the tests
(`<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e:playwright`) in a second one.

| Script                                                  | Description                                  |
| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run playwright`               | Open the Playwright UI mode                  |
| `<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e:playwright`           | Run the suite headless                       |
| `<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e:playwright:headed`    | Run the suite with a visible browser         |
| `<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e:playwright:debug`     | Run the suite with the Playwright inspector  |
| `<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e:playwright:report`    | Open the HTML report of the last run         |

User credentials and the target server can be overridden with environment variables:

```
export E2E_USERNAME="<your-username>"
export E2E_PASSWORD="<your-password>"
export E2E_BASE_URL="http://localhost:<%= gatewayServerPort || serverPort %>/"
```

Traces, screenshots and the HTML report are written to `<%= playwrightTemporaryDir %>`.
<&_ } -&>
<&_ if (fragment.referenceSection) { -&>
[Playwright]: https://playwright.dev/
<&_ } -&>
